{
  "case": "cn-c-unicode-names",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 §3.2 contentSignature; §14.3 Unicode U+E000/U+10000 and whitespace",
  "author": "spec-seal",
  "operation": "complete",
  "profile": "neutral",
  "derivation": "Each ID-less task's contentSignature hashes its exact UTF-8 JCS name with no trim, no NFC and no case folding, so U+E000, U+10000, a leading space, a leading NBSP, the bare name, its lowercase form and Cafe spelled with the precomposed U+00E9 and with the canonically equivalent e + U+0301 give eight distinct signatures, each ordinal 0; an allocator that trims, NFC-normalizes or case-folds merges some of them and gives the later ones nonzero ordinals. Names are preserved. Source targetId is the nearest original ID-bearing ancestor, Process_uni. Report header (H B4): sourceIdentity and targetIdentity are the envelope identity, inputRevision is baseRevision, outputRevision is revision.",
